  "id": "attempt-identity-settle-rederives-downstream",
  "clause": "derive-once-at-ingress",
  "encodes": "The core negative case: identity recomputed downstream from content the facilitator did not capture at ingress.",
  "description": "Three paths take the identity from the ingress snapshot and /settle recomputes it from the request body as it reads it at settle time. The value happens to come out the same here, which is what makes this case worth having: an implementation that only compares values will report conformance, because the defect is in WHERE the value came from, not in what it was this time.",
